ed expression of monocyte chemotactic protein-1 during active hepatic fibrogenesis: correlation with monocyte infiltration</article-title><source>Am J Pathol</source><year>1998</year><volume>152</volume><fpage>423</fpage><lpage>430</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9466568</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hoskins</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Greco</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Pereira</surname><given-names>TN</given-names></name><name><surname>Williamson</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Lewindon</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ramm</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Expression of monocyte chemotaxis protein-1 in paediatric cholestatic liver disease: role in hepatic fibrogenesis</article-title><source>J Gastroenterol Hepatol</source><year>2001</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>A68</fpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>